  "description": "A CLI tool for managing GitHub Projects and Copilot-assigned issues in bulk. Define your project in a YAML file and let orcai create issues, assign them to Copilot, and clean up when done.",
  "id": "OrcAI.Tool",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-03-13T04:41:46.36Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "MvSpRZ4EGbNcUhZtTjM/6vEhPVm5OAV8Q/mG8lCx3jyIeeYk2H73ecQIUzeLCQpk6v3KHNQWdD0NyFu/JCQxtQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 2786140,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/dburriss/orca",
  "published": "2026-03-13T04:38:36.227Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "`orcai validate` command — validates one or more YAML job configs and verifies all listed repos are accessible via `gh repo view`; supports `--json`, `--no-parallel`, `--max-concurrency`, and `--continue-on-error`\nGlob pattern support for `orcai run` and `orcai validate` — pass a quoted glob (e.g. `\"jobs/*.yml\"`) to process multiple config files in one invocation\n`--max-concurrency <n>` flag on `orcai run` and `orcai validate` — limits the number of config files processed concurrently (default: 4); high values may hit GitHub rate limits\n`--no-parallel` flag on `orcai run` and `orcai validate` — disables all parallelism (both file-level and repo-level); overrides `--max-concurrency`\n`--continue-on-error` flag on `orcai run` and `orcai validate` — continues processing remaining files after a failure instead of stopping on the first error\n`--skip-lock` flag on `orcai run` — bypasses the lock file and always fetches live state from GitHub\nLayered config file support — `~/.config/orcai/config.json` (global) and `.orcai/config.json` (local, takes precedence); supports `skipCopilot`, `defaultLabels`, `autoCreateLabels`, `maxConcurrency`, `continueOnError`, and `defaultOrg`\n[BREAKING] `orcai run --json` output shape changed to a filename-keyed object to support multi-file runs; field names also changed: `issuesCreated` → `created`, `issuesAlreadyExisted` → `alreadyExisted`, `issues` → `repos`; a per-file `\"error\"` key is included on failure\n[BREAKING] `orcai validate --json` output is now a filename-keyed object (consistent with `run --json`)\nHuman-readable output for multi-file `run` and `validate` now prefixes each file's output with a `--- <filename> ---` header\nFixed repo accessibility check in validation scripts",
